[38;2;124;124;124mOne more check: I should verify that the "sufficient condition" failing actually[0m[38;2;124;124;124mmeans non-representable, not just that the easy route fails. In step 8, I [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mchecked directly that for n = N, all possible z give either non-representable t [0m[38;2;124;124;124m(k=0, t = Frobenius number) or negative t (k≥1). So N is genuinely not [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mrepresentable. For step 9, I only used the sufficient condition (if R ≥ c(a-1)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(b-1) then representable), which is a valid sufficient condition, so every n > N[0m[38;2;124;124;124mis representable. The fact that some n ≤ N might also be representable (through [0m[38;2;124;124;124msmaller t that happen to be representable) doesn't affect the argument — we only[0m[38;2;124;124;124mneed that N is the LARGEST non-representable.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWait, but in step 6, I said "non-representable (by failing sufficient [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcondition)". This is wrong terminology — failing the sufficient condition [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mdoesn't mean non-representable. Let me rephrase: the set of n that fail the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msufficient condition for a given z₀ are those with n < abc - ac - bc + c + ab·z₀[0m[38;2;124;124;124m(and n ≡ ab·z₀ mod c). Among these, some might still be representable (if t [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mhappens to be a representable number < (a-1)(b-1)). But the point is:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m- Every n > N satisfies the sufficient condition (R ≥ c(a-1)(b-1)), hence IS [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mrepresentable.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- N itself does NOT satisfy the sufficient condition, AND we verified directly [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mit's not representable.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo N is the largest non-representable. The logic is:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- All n > N are representable (sufficient condition).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- N is not representable (direct check).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Therefore N is the largest non-representable.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mI don't need to characterize which n ≤ N are or aren't representable. [0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me write the clean proof now.[0m

